A||||15||theogre||All Users Please Read. New Cave Format Test.||||1||
Z||000000||theogre||04-23-2000||11:12 PM||||As many of you know I write one section of the Fiero.nl web site. I'm working on new information and updates to the site.<P>Herein lies the rub. I've moved to MS Office 2000 and it incorporates a number of things from FrontPage. I need you all to test the new format and tell me if anything breaks.<P>The new format will be framed. I know some people hate that. In this case it does make getting around the information easier. It also makes organization and managment easier for me since I don't need many page custom buttons for it.<P>I think all of the forum readers are now on relatively current versions of Netscape or IE so frames should not ne a problem. (I kept the menu frame as narrow as posible. I can view it comfortably on 800x600 screens on a 15inch monitor.)<P>If part of it fails to work I need to know:<BR>What browser you use and what version it is.<BR>What broke.<BR>What error message if any you got.<P>Notes:<BR>there is a light background image to right frame pages.<BR>The information in the test site has already been updated or is in update process.<P>You can access the test site from this link:<BR><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/ogre/newcave" TARGET=_blank>Ogre Cave Tunnel #6 Test Tube</A><P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-23-2000||11:19 PM||||It's looking great.  I actually like this format much better.  I'm running Netscape 4.7 and it looks fine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-23-2000||11:25 PM||||I'm using win98 second edition with IE 5.00.2314 and I had no problems with the pages. I went thru all the links and everything worked. Looks good! The only thing I'd like to mention is you can take an 84 glass sail panel and it's mounts and use them on an 85 thru 88 notchback. I have an 86 SE and have 84 SE glass sail panels. I noticed in your description you say you can only use glass ones for 84. You can also use the later plastic ones on an 84. The trick is you need the forward metal mounts for the particular sail panel you are installing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||04-23-2000||11:25 PM||||I usually hate frames sites, but yours actually worked! Looks great too. AOL 4.0||||reg||1
